From 9162246409d816a26749e66567be6fbcd9e1a09b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Richard DEMONGEOT <richard@rdem-systems.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 17:32:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 104/120] build: Go 1.26.9 and golang.org/x/net v0.61.0

x/net v0.61.0 fixes the http2 issues govulncheck reports on the PBS
session transport (HPACK encoder race, window-change work, trailer header
limits, double refund on stream close); Go 1.26.9 fixes the reachable
net/http, crypto/tls, mime/multipart, net/textproto and html/template
vulnerabilities of earlier 1.26 releases. x/net >= v0.59 declares go
1.26.0, so the modules that require it, and go.work, move to it.

The go.mod/go.sum changes come from the deps/go-1.26.9 run (go get + go
mod tidy with Go 1.26.9; every module built for linux and windows, vet
clean, tests passing but the token rotator race fixed in the previous
commit). CI, the e2e suite, the ISO build and build_msi_linux.sh pin
1.26.9.

Idea from CJInvent/NimbusBackupClient 2cea7a2 and a3fcbed.
